description:
Hi @saudet ,

Thank you for your effort with this amazing framework!

In order to improve it, I'd like to report about non thread-safe start of multiple recorders. It might be related to issues like #891 since feature **Use locking callback from ffmpeg using a Java locking mechanism. #770** #770 was implemented.

See reproduce code:
```java
import java.io.*;
import java.net.URL;
import java.nio.file.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;

import org.bytedeco.javacpp.avutil;
import org.bytedeco.javacv.*;

public class JavaCVTest {

    private static final String VIDEO_EXAMPLE = "https://www.dropbox.com/s/gilbbjjhft4tzxn/00A8.mp4?dl=1";
    private static final int THREADS = 200;
    private static final int CODEC_CASE = 2;

    private static class WorkerThread implements Runnable {

        private String filePath;
        private int codecCase;

        public WorkerThread(String filePath, int codecCase) {
            this.filePath = filePath;
            this.codecCase = codecCase;
        }

        @Override
        public void run() {
            try (FFmpegFrameGrabber video = new FFmpegFrameGrabber(filePath)) {
                video.start();
                File outputFile = File.createTempFile("video_part_", "_.mp4");
                outputFile.deleteOnExit();
                try (FFmpegFrameRecorder rec = new FFmpegFrameRecorder(outputFile, video.getImageWidth(),
                        video.getImageHeight(), video.getAudioChannels())) {
                    initializeEncoder(video, rec, codecCase);
                    rec.start();
                    Frame frame;
                    if ((frame = video.grab()) != null) {
                        rec.record(frame);
                    }
                } catch (Exception e) {
                    System.err.println(Thread.currentThread().getName() + " : " + e);
                    System.exit(2);
                }
            } catch (Exception e) {
                System.err.println(Thread.currentThread().getName() + " : " + e);
                System.exit(1);
            }
        }

    }

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {

        String filePath = downloadFile(VIDEO_EXAMPLE);

        ExecutorService executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(THREADS);
        for (int i = 0; i < THREADS; i++) {
            Runnable worker = new WorkerThread(filePath, CODEC_CASE);
            executor.execute(worker);
        }
        executor.shutdown();
        while (!executor.isTerminated()) {
            TimeUnit.SECONDS.sleep(1);
        }
        System.out.println("Finished all threads");
    }

    private static String downloadFile(String url) throws IOException {
        File file = new File("source_video.mp4");
        if (!file.exists()) {
            InputStream in = new URL(url).openStream();
            Files.copy(in, file.toPath(), StandardCopyOption.REPLACE_EXISTING);
        }
        return file.getAbsolutePath();
    }

    private static void initializeEncoder(FFmpegFrameGrabber grabber, FFmpegFrameRecorder recorder, int codecCase) {
        // video
        switch (codecCase) {
            case 1:
                recorder.setVideoCodecName("libx264");
                recorder.setVideoOption("profile", "main");
                recorder.setVideoOption("level", "4");
                break;
            case 2:
                // relates to Use locking callback from ffmpeg using a Java locking mechanism. #770
                // https://github.com/bytedeco/javacv/issues/770
                // test https://github.com/bytedeco/javacv/blob/master/platform/src/test/java/org/bytedeco/javacv/FrameGrabberTest.java#L128
                recorder.setPixelFormat(avutil.AV_PIX_FMT_BGR24);
                recorder.setVideoCodecName("libx264rgb");
                break;
            default:
                break;
        }

        recorder.setFrameRate(grabber.getFrameRate());
        recorder.setVideoBitrate(grabber.getVideoBitrate());
        recorder.setVideoOption("threads", "4");
        // audio
        recorder.setSampleRate(grabber.getSampleRate());
        recorder.setAudioBitrate(grabber.getAudioBitrate());
        recorder.setAudioCodec(grabber.getAudioCodec());
    }
}
```
Errors look like:
```
[libx264 @ 0x7f7b381ee300] Codec type or id mismatches
Output #0, mp4, to '/tmp/video_part_6124906312737110217_.mp4':
  Metadata:
    encoder         : Lavf58.20.100
    Stream #0:0: Video: h264 (Constrained Baseline) (avc1 / 0x31637661), yuv420p, 852x480, q=2-31, 988 kb/s, 23.89 fps, 637628 tbn, 23.89 tbc
    Stream #0:1: Audio: aac (LC) (mp4a / 0x6134706D), 44100 Hz, stereo, fltp, 125 kb/s
pool-1-thread-84 : org.bytedeco.javacv.FrameRecorder$Exception: avcodec_open2() error -22: Could not open video codec.
```
**and**

```
[libx264rgb @ 0x7f9b5950a900] Codec type or id mismatches
pool-1-thread-99 : org.bytedeco.javacv.FrameRecorder$Exception: avcodec_open2() error -22: Could not open video codec.
[libx264rgb @ 0x7f9b1c71f580] using cpu capabilities: MMX2 SSE2Fast SSSE3 SSE4.2 AVX FMA3 BMI2 AVX2
[libx264rgb @ 0x7f9b1c71f580] profile High 4:4:4 Predictive, level 3.0, 4:4:4 8-bit
```

My temp solution is to wrap recorders and grabbers, in order to restore commented synchronized functionality by class-object. I mean **start()** and **release()** methods:

```java
/**
     * Keep original thread-safe mechanism, broken since v1.4 (caused exception "avcodec_open2() error -22: Could not
     * open video codec.")
     * @see <a href="https://github.com/bytedeco/javacv/pull/770">Use locking callback from ffmpeg using a Java locking
     * mechanism. #770</a>
     */
    @Override
    public void start() throws Exception {
        synchronized (org.bytedeco.javacpp.avcodec.class) {
            super.start();
        }
    }

    /**
     * Keep original thread-safe mechanism, broken since v1.4 (caused exception "avcodec_open2() error -22: Could not
     * open video codec.")
     * @see <a href="https://github.com/bytedeco/javacv/pull/770">Use locking callback from ffmpeg using a Java locking
     * mechanism. #770</a>
     */
    @Override
    public void release() throws Exception {
        synchronized (org.bytedeco.javacpp.avcodec.class) {
            super.release();
        }
    }
```

Please, try to reproduce it.

