description:
##### Netty Version

Tested with 4.1-CR7 but I think it exists in 4.0 too.
##### Context

I came across this while upgrading [RxNetty](https://github.com/ReactiveX/RxNetty) to netty 4.1-CR7. One of the tests happen to have a more convoluted form of the test specified in this issue.
##### Problem

This [code](https://github.com/netty/netty/blob/4.1/common/src/main/java/io/netty/util/concurrent/DefaultPromise.java#L846) in `DefaultPromise` has the potential to get into an infinite loop where the same task in enqueued repeatedly on the executor. The case happens when there are listeners as well as late listeners for a promise. In such a case when the late listeners are executed via the `LateListeners`task, it never reaches the [point](https://github.com/netty/netty/blob/4.1/common/src/main/java/io/netty/util/concurrent/DefaultPromise.java#L849) to notify the listeners, instead just [executes `self`](https://github.com/netty/netty/blob/4.1/common/src/main/java/io/netty/util/concurrent/DefaultPromise.java#L859) infinitely.
The simplest way to reproduce is with the below reproducer.
##### Reproducer

``` java
        EmbeddedChannel channel = new EmbeddedChannel();
        channel.closeFuture().addListener(new ChannelFutureListener() {
            @Override
            public void operationComplete(ChannelFuture future) throws Exception {
                future.channel().close();
            }
        });

        channel.close().await();
```

The above code will result in an infinite loop due to the above explained issue.

description_code:
``` java
        EmbeddedChannel channel = new EmbeddedChannel();
        channel.closeFuture().addListener(new ChannelFutureListener() {
            @Override

                future.channel().close();
            }
        });

        channel.close().await();
```

```
public class Netty4Deadlock {

    private static final Logger logger = LoggerFactory.getLogger(Netty4Deadlock.class);


        DefaultChannelGroup channels = new DefaultChannelGroup(GlobalEventExecutor.INSTANCE);
        Bootstrap bootstrap = new Bootstrap();
        NioEventLoopGroup group = new NioEventLoopGroup();
        bootstrap.group(group);
        bootstrap.channel(NioSocketChannel.class);
        bootstrap.option(ChannelOption.CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MILLIS, 10000);
        bootstrap.handler(new LoggingHandler());

        //nothing running on the port 5000
        ChannelFuture connectFuture = bootstrap.connect(new InetSocketAddress("localhost", 5000));

        destroy(channels, group);

        logger.info("isDone={}", connectFuture.isDone()); //false
        logger.info("isCancelled={}", connectFuture.isCancelled()); //false
        logger.info("deadlock here:");
        connectFuture.awaitUninterruptibly();
        logger.info("done"); //never gets here
    }

    private static void destroy(DefaultChannelGroup channels, NioEventLoopGroup workerGroup) {
        logger.info("destroy");
        channels.close().awaitUninterruptibly();

        workerGroup.shutdownGracefully();

        try {
            // Wait until all threads are terminated.
            workerGroup.terminationFuture().sync();

            logger.warn("Thread interrupted closing executors.", e);
        }
    }
}
